y the product of the diagonal entries.\n\n- For the second determinant, we can compute it using a Laplace expansion down the ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14050601/assets/c23fa2f99aef303059a834682e511943ffbe022294cf2d9ac8e72e707316a607.png)st column.\n\nTherefore, we obtain \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14050601/assets/b968eb1cf6b8a72d8f4b46202ea1a6ab201145ae2531bfe2b5a2049aafae9b28.png)" 13194139535052 true] [17592186119519 1145 "Given two $n\\times n$ matrices $A$ and $B$, we have\n\n$$\n\\det(AB) = \\det(A)\\cdot \\det(B)\n$$\n\nIn our case, this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ndet(A) &= det\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 11 \\\\ 0 & -\\sqrt{3} & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\sqrt{3}\\end{bmatrix} \\cdot det\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 1 & -\\sqrt{11} \\\\ 0 & 5 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 4 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can compute the required determinants as follows:\n\n- For the first determinant, we notice that it's upper triangular. Therefore, the determinant is simply the product of the diagonal entries.\n- For the second determinant, we can compute it using a Laplace expansion down the $1$st column.\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ndet(A) &= \\begin{vmatrix}1 & 2 & 11 \\\\ 0 & -\\sqrt{3} & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\sqrt{3}\\end{vmatrix}\\cdot\\begin{vmatrix}-2 & 1 & -\\sqrt{11} \\\\ 0 & 5 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 4 & -1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\\n&= (1 \\cdot (-\\sqrt{3}) \\cdot 3\\sqrt{3}) \\cdot (-2(-1)^{1 + 1}\\begin{vmatrix}5 & -1 \\\\ 4 & -1\\end{vmatrix}) \\\\\n&= (-9) \\cdot ((-2) \\cdot (-5 + 4)) \\\\\n&= (-9) \\cdot 2 \\\\\n&=-18\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535052 false] [17592186119520 1100 "Find $\\mid A^{-1} \\mid$, if $\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 14 & -1 \\\\ 7 & -6 & -6 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$" 13194139535052 false] [17592186119520 1100 "Find $|A^{-1}|,$ if  ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14050601/assets/8a5169c6a418a8ddaa9b3478e535039b253724ae622692ea728b2a94dc112e4a.png)" 13194139535052 true] [17592186119520 1145 "Given an invertible $n\\times n$ matrix $A$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{vmatrix}A^{-1} & = \\dfrac{1}{\\mid A\\end{vmatrix}}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find $\\mid A \\mid$ using a Laplace expansion across the $3$rd row:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\begin{vmatrix}A & &= & 2 & 14\\end{vmatrix}- 1 \\\\\n&= 7\\begin{vmatrix}-6 & -6 \\\\ 0 & -3\\end{vmatrix}0 \\mid \\\\\n&=-3(-1)^{3 + 2}\\begin{vmatrix}2 & -1 \\\\ 7 & -6\\end{vmatrix} \\\\\n&= 3 \\cdot (-12 + 7) \\\\\n&=-15\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\det(A^{-1}) = \\dfrac{1}{\\mid A \\mid} = -\\dfrac{1}{15}\n$$" 13194139535052 false] [17592186119520 1145 "Given an invertible $n\\times n$ matrix $A,$ we have\n\n$$\n|A^{-1}| = \\dfrac{1}{|A|}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find $|A|$ using a Laplace expansion across the $3$rd row:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|A| & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & 14 & -1 \\\\ 7 & -6 & -6 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-3(-1)^{3+2}|\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 7 & -6\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =3\\cdot (-12+7) \\\\  & =-15\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\det(A^{-1}) =  \\dfrac{1}{|A|} = -\\dfrac{1}{15}.\n$$" 13194139535052 true] [17592186119521 1100 "Given that\n$\\begin{vmatrix}a & b & c \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2\\end{vmatrix}$\nfind\n$\\begin{vmatrix}a & b & c + 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2\\end{vmatrix}$" 13194139535052 false] [17592186119521 1100 "Given that \n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14050601/assets/96eacd1217f27ffb734d64453ac3fca3cac6124a781dcd677c898ec4a4317427.png)\nfind \n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14050601/assets/64009b40661083c1e152b6277f329c6e22a0588fc0b3fd3d08db5e51ace0b27d.png)" 13194139535052 true] [17592186119521 1145 "We \"factor out\" the given determinant from the determinant we would like to find:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\begin{vmatrix}a & b & c + 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2\\end{vmatrix} &= \\begin{vmatrix}a + 0 & b + 0 & c + 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2\\end{vmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the linearity property of determinants and expanding the second determinant across the $1$st row, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\begin{vmatrix}a + 0 & b + 0 & c + 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2\\end{vmatrix} &= \\begin{vmatrix}a & b & c \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2\\end{vmatrix}_(⏟)_(-10) +\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\\n&=-10 + 1(-1)^{1 + 3}\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\\n&=-10 - 1 \\\\\n&=-11\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535052 false] [17592186119521 1145 "We \"factor out\" the given determinant from the determinant we would like to find:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}a & b & c+1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}| & =|\\begin{aligned}a+0 & b+0 & c+1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the linearity property of determinants and expanding the second determinant across the $1$st row, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}a+0 & b+0 & c+1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}| & ={{|\\begin{aligned}a & b & c \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}|}_{⏟}}_{-10}+|\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-10+1(-1)^{1+3}|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-10-1 \\\\  & =-11.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535052 true] [17592186119702 1020 #edb/ref 17592186328541 13194139535052 true] [17592186119702 1020 #edb/ref 17592186328548 13194139535052 true] [17592186119702 1020 #edb/ref 17592186328555 13194139535052 true] [17592186119702 1020 #edb/ref 17592186328562 13194139535052 true] [17592186119702 1020 #edb/ref 17592186328604 13194139535052 true] [17592186119703 1020 #edb/ref 17592186328569 13194139535052 true] [17592186119703 1020 #edb/ref 17592186328576 13194139535052 true] [17592186119703 1020 #edb/ref 17592186328597 13194139535052 true] [17592186119704 1020 #edb/ref 17592186328583 13194139535052 true] [17592186119704 1020 #edb/ref 17592186328590 13194139535052 true] [17592186119704 1020 #edb/ref 17592186328611 13194139535052 true] [17592186119704 1020 #edb/ref 17592186328618 13194139535052 true] [17592186120362 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535052 true] [17592186120362 1100 "Given that\n\n$\\mid a + 3\\begin{vmatrix}-5 \\\\ b\\end{vmatrix}6|=-7$,\nfind\n$\\begin{vmatrix}a + 2 & -5 \\\\ b + 4 & 6\\end{vmatrix}$." 13194139535052 false] [17592186120362 1100 "Given that \n$|\\begin{aligned}a+3 & -5 \\\\ b & 6\\end{aligned}|=-7$,\nfind \n$|\\begin{aligned}a+2 & -5 \\\\ b+4 & 6\\end{aligned}|.$" 13194139535052 true] [17592186120362 1145 "We \"factor out\" the given determinant from the determinant we would like to find:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}a+2 & -5 \\\\ b+4 & 6\\end{aligned}| & =|\\begin{aligned}(a+3)-1 & -5 \\\\ b+4 & 6\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the linearity property of determinants, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}(a+3)-1 & -5 \\\\ b+4 & 6\\end{aligned}| & ={{|\\begin{aligned}a+3 & -5 \\\\ b & 6\\end{aligned}|}_{⏟}}_{-7}+|\\begin{aligned}-1 & -5 \\\\ 4 & 6\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-7+(-6+20) \\\\  & =7.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535052 true] [17592186120363 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535052 true] [17592186120363 1100 "Find $\\mid A^{-1} \\mid$, if $A = \\begin{bmatrix}-5 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 1 & -2 \\\\ -6 & -2 & 3\\end{bmatrix}$." 13194139535052 false] [17592186120363 1100 "Find $|{A}^{-1}|,$ if $A=[\\begin{aligned}-5 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 1 & -2 \\\\ -6 & -2 & 3\\end{aligned}].$" 13194139535052 true] [17592186120363 1145 "Given an invertible $n\\times n$ matrix $A,$ we have\n\n$$\n|{A}^{-1}|=\\frac{1}{|A|}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find $|A|$ using a Laplace expansion across the $2$nd column:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|A| & =|\\begin{aligned}-5 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 1 & -2 \\\\ -6 & -2 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-1(-1)^{1+2}|\\begin{aligned}4 & -2 \\\\ -6 & 3\\end{aligned}|+1(-1)^{2+2}|\\begin{aligned}-5 & 4 \\\\ -6 & 3\\end{aligned}|-2(-1)^{3+2}|\\begin{aligned}-5 & 4 \\\\ 4 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(12-12)+(-15+24)+2(10-16) \\\\  & =0+9-12 \\\\  & =-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain \n\n$$\n|{A}^{-1}|=\\frac{1}{|A|}=-\\frac{1}{3}.\n$$" 13194139535052 true] [17592186120378 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535052 true] [17592186120378 1100 "Find $det(A^{-1})$, if $A = \\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 6\\end{bmatrix}$." 13194139535052 false] [17592186120378 1100 "Find $det({A}^{-1}),$ if $A=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 6\\end{aligned}].$" 13194139535052 true] [17592186120378 1145 "Given an invertible $n\\times n$ matrix $A,$ we have\n\n$$\ndet({A}^{-1})=\\frac{1}{det(A)}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find $det(A):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =det[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =12+3 \\\\  & =15\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain \n\n$$\ndet({A}^{-1})=\\frac{1}{det(A)}=\\frac{1}{15}.\n$$" 13194139535052 true] [17592186328541 1017 #edb/ref 17592186328542 13194139535052 true] [17592186328541 1089 "q-130484" 13194139535052 true] [17592186328541 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535052 true] [17592186328541 1100 "Given that $Q=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 7 & 5 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 9 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 & 5 & 6 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}],$ find $det(Q).$" 13194139535052 true] [17592186328541 1113 #uuid "7f1e9143-c8f8-54c0-8457-88cd22fe54aa" 13194139535052 true] [17592186328541 1145 "Given two $n\\times n$ matrices $M$ and $N,$ we have\n\n$$\ndet(MN)=det(M)\\cdot det(N).\n$$\n\nIn our case, this gives\n\n$$\ndet(Q)=det[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 7 & 5 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 9 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot det[\\begin{aligned}3 & 5 & 6 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNotice that both matrices are triangular. Therefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(Q) & =(4\\cdot 5\\cdot (-1))\\cdot (3\\cdot (-2)\\cdot 2) \\\\  & =(-20)\\cdot (-12) \\\\  & =240.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535052 true] [17592186328542 1000 #edb/ref 17592186328543 13194139535052 true] [17592186328542 1000 #edb/ref 17592186328544 13194139535052 true] [17592186328542 1000 #edb/ref 17592186328545 13194139535052 true] [17592186328542 1000 #edb/ref 17592186328546 13194139535052 true] [17592186328542 1000 #edb/ref 17592186328547 13194139535052 true] [17592186328542 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535052 true] [17592186328542 1041 "selection" 13194139535052 true] [17592186328542 1104 #edb/ref 17592186328544 13194139535052 true] [17592186328542 1110 #uuid "0f555972-c1a1-5877-a2d6-e4e2d2f91eeb" 13194139535052 true] [17592186328543 1034 "220" 13194139535052 true] [17592186328543 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535052 true] [17592186328543 1111 #uuid "056c84ca-82fc-5af2-b63f-6618e6d6129d" 13194139535052 true] [17592186328544 1034 "240" 13194139535052 true] [17592186328544 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535052 true] [17592186328544 1111 #uuid "8166199f-1021-5bdd-ad31-d4420d9b14e1" 13194139535052 true] [17592186328545 1034 "204" 13194139535052 true] [17592186328545 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535052 true] [17592186328545 1111 #uuid "90255b74-e153-57a7-bce5-7f42236db6c4" 13194139535052 true] [17592186328546 1034 "-120" 13194139535052 true] [17592186328546 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535052 true] [17592186328546 1111 #uuid "36ebd86d-6964-513a-84ac-dfdbe713bf3e" 13194139535052 true] [17592186328547 1034 "-224" 13194139535052 true] [17592186328547 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535052 true] [17592186328547 1111 #uuid "db4e3ac3-c49a-5b7c-b1b6-8da393e1bac4" 13194139535052 true] [17592186328548 1017 #edb/ref 17592186328549 13194139535052 true] [17592186328548 1089 "q-130488" 13194139535052 true] [17592186328548 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535052 true] [17592186328548 1100 "Given that 